+# OPEN A, LOUD FAILURE. A wave that has made no progress for this many seconds
+# KILLS THE ENGINE instead of retrying forever. Observed on a build of this
+# profile: a wave whose source files did not exist on disk retried ~1.6M times
+# over 95 minutes -- engine pinned at ~170% CPU, 97% of GPU KV held, nothing
+# served, and the client's 15-minute resends walked into the same hole six
+# times. A dead engine is visible; that was not.
+#
+# Why a crash and not recompute: falling back means reporting this request's
+# still-unloaded GPU blocks as failed loads so vLLM recomputes them, which runs
+# through the worker-side load-error path on EVERY rank, and whether vLLM
+# re-enters cleanly on already-allocated blocks has not been verified.
+# Unverified KV reuse produces garbage output; a crash cannot.
+#
+# Why 120 s is safe: over 16 days of production journal, no wave outside that
+# incident ever reached even MAX_WAVE_PROMOTE_RETRIES (50 steps).
+# 0 = retry forever (the previous behaviour).
+WAVE_STUCK_S = float(os.environ.get("VLLM_OFFLOAD_STREAM_WAVE_STUCK_S", "120") or 0)
